Subject: Question: Seasonal Affective Disorder

>Charlie Stross says:
>> I'm pretty certain that I suffer from a syndrome called SAD; seasonal
>> affective disorder.
>[...]

It's a bitch!

I remember when I was at Michigan State that a fair amount of research was
being done on SAD. East Lansing gets about 5-6 months of gray, cloudy days
from  late October to April with hardly any sunshine. It's a good place for
this type of research.

As I recall, the researchers found that both light intensity (very high),
light frequencies (tuned somewhat into the pink [yea I know how that
sounds]) and scheduling (early enough in the AM to kick in the circadian
rhythms) seemed to show significant success for people with S.A.D.
depression and eating disorders.

My solution: I moved to sunny California from ugly, gray and dank Michigan.
